domain SemanticAuthoringDesignRevision5SelfCheck:
  description "Check revision five against the two revision-four P1 findings without accepting it."
problem P1:
  |
    Determine whether revision five preserves the matching cumulative-resource outcome
    and closes the no-valid-recovery-basis path without choosing pending numeric policy
    or changing unrelated architecture.
evidence E0:
  |
    The exact English revision-five candidate SHA256 is
    426470047d0e380de90624192b9db71d3f30788fa44423ed0710f9cb1e6cdba4.
    Its complete Japanese projection SHA256 is
    7130a67b9e13521d072c7c10cb5d3c1d4bb2bcf08268322b22765ac4596434a0.
evidence E1:
  |
    Revision five section 7.2 makes transport-recovery eligibility precede cumulative-
    resource admission. Zero recovery, consumed recovery, and absence of a truthful
    server-derived recovery basis terminate as recoverable provider transport
    unavailability with distinct reasons and an owner new-run recipe.
evidence E2:
  |
    Revision five section 7.2 performs cumulative-resource admission only for an
    otherwise-eligible recovery. Failed admission terminates as resource_exhausted,
    identifies every exhausted cumulative dimension and consumed or retained-reservation
    accounting, and is explicitly not relabeled as provider unavailability.
evidence E3:
  |
    Both failure branches retain the source timeout receipt and monotonic accounting,
    do not assert semantic invalidity, and do not reset or start another attempt.
evidence E4:
  |
    Revision five section 10 parameterizes zero, consumed, no-basis, and otherwise-
    eligible resource-admission failure. It requires the first three to reach provider
    transport unavailability, the fourth to reach resource_exhausted with exact
    dimensions and accounting, and all paths to reject blind replay.
premise C1:
  |
    This self-check does not provide fresh independent review or exact owner acceptance.
premise U1:
  |
    Exact provider timeout, worker lease, and selection of zero or one transport
    recovery remain pending under ADR-0032.
decision D1 based_on P1, E0, E1, E2, E3, E4:
  |
    Revision five closes both revision-four P1 findings with deterministic transition
    precedence and matching conformance obligations.
decision D2 based_on P1, E1, E2, C1, U1:
  |
    Keep cc304 suspended and present exact revision five for fresh independent REVIEW.
    Do not infer design acceptance, implementation, route activation, or numeric-policy
    selection from this self-check.
